content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-111 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-21100",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 4.2 mm/s: treating this as the required bearing-housing RMS velocity, it falls in Zone B, 2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, labelled 'Long-term operation'. It is below the 4.5 mm/s Zone C boundary (restricted—plan maintenance) and below the 7.1 mm/s Zone C/D boundary; it is not in Zone D, labelled 'Damage likely—stop the pump'. Measurements on both housings and classification of the highest reading are required.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Housing temperature 74 °C is 4 °C above the documented normal upper limit of 70 °C, but remains 6 °C below the 80 °C alarm and 16 °C below the 90 °C trip. The applicable assessment is therefore above normal, not at alarm or trip. Housing-surface measurement is the documented measurement basis.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Grinding noise from the non-drive-end bearing independently meets the manual's bearing-replacement trigger: replace both bearings as a pair when either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature. Zone B vibration does not remove this noise-based replacement requirement.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No documented immediate-stop criterion is established by the supplied numerical readings: vibration is below the Zone C/D boundary and temperature is below both alarm and trip. P2 planned corrective repair is appropriate for the noisy bearing and above-normal temperature rather than an emergency stop based solely on these readings.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The report's statement that the seal is 'dry' does not establish whether it means no external leakage or actual dry running. The operating specification requires Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and says never run dry; the troubleshooting seal-replacement action is tied to leakage at the shaft seal. Seal failure or replacement scope cannot be confirmed from the wording alone.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Leading suspect: non-drive-end bearing wear or damage. The localized grinding noise and above-normal housing temperature support bearing investigation, and bearing wear is documented as a cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature. Regardless of the final root cause, the noise already requires replacement of the bearing pair.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment is the next common documented cause to check because it can produce both high vibration and high bearing temperature; the troubleshooting table requires an alignment check.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing may contribute to the above-normal bearing temperature. Check grease quantity; this documented cause does not by itself explain all the reported symptoms.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage and cavitation remain documented alternative causes of high vibration. Inspect the impeller and check NPSH before closing the repair.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before disassembly, confirm that the 4.2 mm/s reading is RMS vibration velocity, identify its housing, measure both bearing housings, and classify the highest result using Figure 3. Record housing-surface temperatures and compare them with the 70/80/90 °C limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before the documented back-pull-out/seal disassembly. If the back pull-out assembly is removed, use lifting equipment: its mass is 68 kg. The back pull-out design allows removal of the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Investigate the causes before reassembly: check grease quantity, inspect the bearings and impeller, check NPSH, and check shaft alignment. Record the findings rather than assuming bearing wear is the sole cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace both bearings as a pair because the non-drive-end bearing is noisy: HF3-510, non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3, and HF3-512, drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Use the applicable detailed bearing removal/installation procedure; those detailed steps are not included in the supplied evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not automatically replace the seal solely on the ambiguous word 'dry'. If shaft-seal leakage is confirmed and seal replacement is authorized, follow procedure 5.2: remove the impeller nut and impeller, withdraw the seal and sleeve, inspect the sleeve for scoring, and fit a new HF3-450 component seal and new casing gasket. HF3-450 is the applicable seal for this serial if replacement is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket whenever the casing is opened. For fasteners actually disturbed, use Table 5 with lightly oiled threads: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm; M24 impeller nut 160 Nm if removed; M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm; and M10 seal gland nuts 25 Nm if seal work is performed. The bulletin's 30 Nm gland torque does not apply to this serial.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before running the pump, confirm Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and do not run the seal dry. Following the work, repeat vibration measurements on both bearing housings, classify the highest result, and recheck housing-surface temperature against the documented limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3, item 6; required because the reported noisy bearing triggers replacement of both bearings as a pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3, item 5; replace together with HF3-510 as a matched maintenance pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket, item 8; fit new whenever the casing is opened and when performing the documented seal-replacement procedure.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450",
      "description": "CONTINGENT ONLY: component-type mechanical seal, item 3, if seal replacement is separately confirmed. This is the applicable seal for serial HF3-21100; do not substitute HF3-450B under SB-2026-014.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before the documented back-pull-out/seal disassembly sequence.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and never run the pump seal dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If subsequent vibration is classified in Zone D, follow the figure's instruction: damage is likely and the pump is to be stopped. The supplied 4.2 mm/s reading is not in that zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair: standard allowance 6.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 12 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 hours with 1 technician whenever the repair moves the motor or bearing housing; section 5.4 makes alignment mandatory after such movement.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional seal scope only: if mechanical seal replacement is separately confirmed, the standard allowance is 4.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 8 technician-hours. Do not include this in the bearing-only scope by default.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part and gland torque: the manual lists component seal HF3-450 and Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts. SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, instead specifies HF3-450B and 30 Nm, but only for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. Asset HF3-21100 is below that range, and the bulletin explicitly says pumps below HF3-22000 continue using HF3-450 and manual Table 5. Therefore, if seal work is required on this asset, use HF3-450 and 25 Nm with lightly oiled threads, not HF3-450B or 30 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-sleeve instructions also differ by serial range. The bulletin says HF3-450B is pre-set with no sleeve measurement needed and gives a 0.1 mm scoring-depth replacement criterion, but those instructions are within its HF3-22000-and-above scope. For HF3-21100, follow the manual instruction to withdraw and inspect HF3-455 for scoring if the seal is replaced; do not treat the bulletin's 0.1 mm criterion as the documented limit for this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Does 'seal is dry' mean no visible external leakage, or that the seal has actually run dry or lost its Plan 11 flush? Is there any leakage, flush-system fault or dry-running history? This determines whether the contingent HF3-450 seal and additional labour are required.",
    "Was the reported 4.2 mm/s measured as RMS velocity on a bearing housing, which housing was measured, and what was the reading on the other housing? C06 requires both housings to be measured and the highest reading classified.",
    "Does 74 °C apply to both bearing housings or only one? Record the location-specific temperatures, grease quantity and condition to resolve the temperature contributor.",
    "What are the alignment, NPSH/cavitation and impeller-inspection findings? The supplied report is insufficient to establish the underlying root cause beyond the noisy bearing's replacement trigger.",
    "The supplied bearing-replacement section only mandates pair replacement; it does not provide detailed removal/installation steps, bearing fits, lubricant specification or grease quantity. Obtain the applicable procedure and lubrication requirements before bearing installation.",
    "If seal replacement exposes shaft-sleeve scoring, what acceptance/rejection criterion applies below serial HF3-22000? The manual requires inspection but supplies no numerical limit, and SB-2026-014's 0.1 mm criterion is scoped to HF3-22000 and above."
  ]
}
